🐍 Python Practice – If-Else Statements

This section contains basic to intermediate if-else problems with their solutions.
A great way to strengthen your Python fundamentals 🚀

✅ 1. Check Even or Odd
num = 7

if num % 2 == 0:
    print("Even")
else:
    print("Odd")
# Output: Odd

✅ 2. Age Category
age = 25

if age < 18:
    print("Minor")
elif age < 60:
    print("Adult")
else:
    print("Senior Citizen")
# Output: Adult

✅ 3. Positive, Negative or Zero
num = -5

if num > 0:
    print("Positive")
elif num < 0:
    print("Negative")
else:
    print("Zero")
# Output: Negative

✅ 4. Divisible by 5
num = 20

if num % 5 == 0:
    print("Divisible by 5")
else:
    print("Not divisible by 5")
# Output: Divisible by 5

✅ 5. Greater Number
a, b = 12, 8

if a > b:
    print("Greater number is:", a)
else:
    print("Greater number is:", b)
# Output: Greater number is: 12

✅ 6. Leap Year Check
year = 2024

if (year % 4 == 0 and year % 100 != 0) or (year % 400 == 0):
    print("Leap Year")
else:
    print("Not a Leap Year")
# Output: Leap Year

✅ 7. Grading System
marks = 82

if marks >= 90:
    print("Grade A")
elif marks >= 75:
    print("Grade B")
elif marks >= 50:
    print("Grade C")
else:
    print("Fail")
# Output: Grade B

✅ 8. Number in Range
num = 55

if 1 <= num <= 100:
    print("Number is in range 1 to 100")
else:
    print("Out of range")
# Output: Number is in range 1 to 100

✅ 9. Largest of Three
a, b, c = 45, 72, 19

if a >= b and a >= c:
    print("Largest:", a)
elif b >= a and b >= c:
    print("Largest:", b)
else:
    print("Largest:", c)
# Output: Largest: 72

✅ 10. Voting Eligibility
age = 16

if age >= 18:
    print("Eligible to vote")
else:
    print("Not eligible to vote")
# Output: Not eligible to vote

✅ 11. Password Check
password = "Python123"

if password == "Python123":
    print("Access Granted")
else:
    print("Access Denied")
# Output: Access Granted

✅ 12. Divisible by 3 and 7
num = 21

if num % 3 == 0 and num % 7 == 0:
    print("Divisible by both 3 and 7")
else:
    print("Not divisible by both")
# Output: Divisible by both 3 and 7

✅ 13. Temperature Category
temp = 30

if temp < 0:
    print("Freezing")
elif temp <= 20:
    print("Cold")
elif temp <= 35:
    print("Warm")
else:
    print("Hot")
# Output: Warm

✅ 14. Vowel or Consonant
char = "e"

if char.lower() in "aeiou":
    print("Vowel")
else:
    print("Consonant")
# Output: Vowel

✅ 15. Two-Digit Number
num = 45

if 10 <= num <= 99:
    print("Two-digit number")
else:
    print("Not a two-digit number")
# Output: Two-digit number
